sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — MorphoEval overall 67.7/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The script implements the Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) orientation-hypercolumn model in recognisable form: the exact two-regime retino-cortical map with the paper's w0 and eps and an analytic inverse, Fourier-Bessel lateral harmonics with the sin(2n theta0)/(2n theta0) spread factor, even/odd perturbative dispersion curves to O(beta^2), cubic normal-form stability tests (roll stable iff 2 gamma3(theta) > gamma0) and the tangent map phi_R = phi + theta_R for line elements. Its numerical parity is with the vendored MesmerPrism Rust port (max |diff| 2.2e-16 on 5 stability_reports and 24 runs), which is stated plainly; the fixture's 12 failed paper- expectation checks, the alpha/lambda_c discrepancies and the Rule (2011) calibration_claim_allowed=false status are disclosed in the ledger, CSV and self-test rather than hidden. The remaining substantive gaps are that the cubic coefficients are bare eigenfunction overlap integrals, contoured vs non-contoured is a preset flag rather than a derived W0/W1 criterion, no swept model parameter changes the selected lattice family (rhombic everywhere), the rendered wavelength is 3.1x the paper's perceptual estimate, and the full-field spiral carries a seam spanning most of the 40 deg disc. Rendering is byte-identical across runs and pinned to a lock file. Overall 67.7/100 (faithfulness 61.7, reproducibility 81.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d6f3c94; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 70, Morphological realism / specimen match 63, Parameter expressivity 52, Morphometric validation 55, Source and data traceability 84, Code-to-model traceability 72, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at d6f3c94, image/png, 1634872 B, 2620×2419 px, artifact_sha256 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e (sha256 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; artifact_sha256: 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bressloff/driven-neural-fields-registry.json=4f07b5175a48bcb5..., datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json=af12b2c1aa3e38fa..., datasets/bressloff/rule-2011-floquet.json=5e349c7b80185de4...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even (contoured) and odd (non-contoured) planforms, pulled back through the retino-cortical map x=(alpha/eps)ln(1+eps r/w0), y=beta r theta/(w0+eps r), give Klüver's four form constants; the 2002 paper states a foveal magnification of 11.5 mm/deg, 30-36 perceived stripes and a cortical wavelength of 2.4-3.2 mm | Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map | Horton & Hoyt (1991): human V1 linear cortical magnification follows M(E) = 17.3/(E + 0.75) mm/deg | Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number | Tamekue, Prandi & Chitour (2024): a Gaussian-only (no Mexican-hat) lateral kernel produces no MacKay-type pattern, used here as the negative control; reconstructed_in_script: Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling, even/odd orientation eigenbranches and marginal-stability scans, cubic amplitude-equation coefficients gamma_0, gamma_3(theta), eta_hex with unrestricted branch selection (rhombic angle = argmin gamma_3) and per-panel SELECTED / STABLE-coexisting / IMPOSED-unstable badges, the exact two-regime retino-cortical map with analytic inverse in a full-field theta in (-pi, pi] convention (bilateral-mirror mode kept and compared, seam contrast and mirror symmetry quantified), an orientation field drawn as line elements in cortex and in the visual field via the tangent map phi_R = phi + theta_R, rendered wavenumber |k| = q*/d_hyp quantised to integer torus cycles, exact parity with all 5 stability_reports and all 24 preset runs of the upstream fixture with all 133 of its paper-expectation checks counted (121 pass), a comparison of the map's magnification with Horton & Hoyt (1991) and with the 2002 paper's own scale anchors, parameter sweeps over lateral width, lateral inhibition and lateral spread (CLI --sweep), a Gaussian-only negative control cross-referenced to the vendored registry, and a diagnostic overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries (16 curves over 5 forcing amplitudes) vendored from the upstream MesmerPrism fixture with its calibration status printed; transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to 2.2e-16 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports and runs, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper; alpha = 3/pi and beta = 1.589/2 are the upstream params.rs values (foveal magnification 10.98 vs the paper's 11.5 mm/deg) and the rendered cortical wavelength 8.7 mm is 3.1x the paper's 2.4-3.2 mm — both are computed and printed, not corrected | Of the five gallery panels only the rhombic lattice is SELECTED by the cubic amplitude equations; the honeycomb is STABLE-coexisting and tunnel/spiral/cobweb are IMPOSED-unstable, because the bare orientation-overlap cubic coefficients make 2 gamma_3(theta*) < gamma_0 for every parameter value swept (rolls and squares never stable) | The full-field pullback carries a discontinuity on the left horizontal meridian (seam contrast 7-10x for oblique modes) because the theta in (-pi, pi] branch cut maps to a line in cortex; the bilateral-mirror alternative removes the seam but destroys spiral chirality (mirror symmetry 1.000); does_not_claim: Fifth-order resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy (Bressloff 2001 Section 5.2), the full cubic coefficients with firing-rate derivative weights and quadratic feedback (Eq. 5.15), a Floquet solver or validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream and the script says so), derivation of contoured vs non-contoured from the critical local harmonic (contour_mode is a preset flag), or a comparison with subject drawings of hallucinations." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:131-132, 305-306, 309 and 949-958 — alpha = 3/pi and lateral widths xi = 1, xi_hat = 1.5 are upstream choices that give lambda_c = 8.7 mm (3.1x the paper's 2.4-3.2 mm) and 11 rings vs 30-36 stripes, and stability_q_max = 3.5 makes the paper's q* ~ 4.5 unreachable. Add a paper-scale preset (q scan to ~5, or d_hyp consistent with lambda_c ~ 2d) rendered beside the parity preset so the discrepancy is tested, not only reported.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:1506-1560 with bressloff_v1_metrics.csv parameter_sweep rows — the unrestricted cubic selection is 'rhombic' at every point of all three sweeps, so no swept model parameter changes the form-constant family; the tunnel/spiral/cobweb/honeycomb axis is the categorical pattern string and pattern_angle_deg at lines 982-1013. Either add a sweep (e.g. eigen_beta or local_sigma_deg across a range where the selected lattice changes) with pullbacks rendered along it, or state in Panel F/G that the family is not parameter-controlled.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:2487-2493 and 2576-2580 — the Horton & Hoyt acceptance threshold (25% RMS) passes a 30% maximum relative error and E2 = 1.71 vs 0.75 deg, and the k* check compares the FFT ring with the rendered cycle count derived from the same q* (circular). Tighten the magnification test to the paper's own 11.5 mm/deg and 5.75 mm/deg anchors and add a retinal morphometric (rings per degree, spiral pitch, cobweb spoke count) compared with Klüver's or Bressloff Fig. 1 observations.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:291, 1062, 1070-1076 and 592-599 — contour_mode is a preset flag; the paper's contoured vs non-contoured dichotomy is whether the n = 0 (Hubel-Wiesel) or n = 1 local harmonic is critical (W0 vs W1), but branch_growth always uses W1 as its base. Derive contour_mode from argmax_n of the critical growth over n in {0, 1} so Figs. 29-30 non-contoured planforms are selected rather than imposed.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:686-695 — amplitude_gamma3 integrates only u^2(phi - theta) u^2(phi) with unit cubic gain; Bressloff 2001 Eq. 5.15 also carries the firing-rate derivative weights and quadratic-feedback terms, so the 'rolls and squares never stable' verdict at lines 811-818 and every SELECTED/IMPOSED badge rest on a reduced functional. Implement the full coefficient or relabel gamma3 as the bare overlap integral in the docstring, ledger and badges.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:74-76 and 1102-1107 — the full-field theta in (-pi, pi] convention leaves a gap L/2 - y(pi) of 0.82 wavelengths at 10 deg, 1.43 at 5 deg and 0.23 at 40 deg, so the 9.9x seam spans most of the 40 deg disc (visible in the PNG spiral panel and GIF frame 8), not 'near the fovea' as the docstring says. Fix: in bilateral-mirror mode negate pattern_angle_deg for the left hemisphere (reflect the wavevector, not the mode) so chiral spirals stay continuous without a seam, and correct the docstring.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:982-1013 — planform_modes hard-codes phase multipliers 0.35 and -0.25 and an amplitude of -1 on one hex_pi mode without citation; cos(k1.r) - cos(k2.r) + cos(k3.r) is not the paper's H_pi (a translate of H_0 with all phases pi). Cite the source of each multiplier or replace hex_pi with the Eq. 5.17 definition.",
            "remediation needed: README.md:432 and 437-441 — stale against the code: '--self-test runs 17 checks ... in ~3 s' (27 PASS lines, ~12 s), 'the same four presets' and '1/4 ... 4/4' (GIF shows five presets labelled n/5), and 'both hemispheres carry the same bilateral eigenmode so the vertical meridian is continuous' although the default hemifield_mode is full-field (line 297). Update the section to the current CLI, preset count and default convention.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:1080-1092 — _eval_xy selects the contoured orientation via np.abs(val) > np.abs(best) (argmax_phi |a(x, phi)|) rather than signed activity argmax_phi a(x, phi), causing discontinuous sign flips across nodal lines that shift the contoured hexagonal FFT peak to the 2k harmonic (21 cycles vs 11 linear cycles).",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:1156-1172 — retinal_pullback_diagnostics computes seam_contrast from |f[cy] - f[cy-1]| across v = 0, which vanishes identically on both meridians for any y-even planform at phase = 0 (Cobweb and Honeycomb), returning NaN and mislabelling both panels as 'seam n/a (y-independent)' at line 1957.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:672-695 — amplitude_gamma2 and amplitude_gamma3 compute only local orientation overlap integrals without the spatial lateral-kernel weighting, quadratic-mode feedback, or quintic terms of Bressloff et al. (2001 §5, Eqs. 5.12-5.15), so rolls and squares are never stable anywhere in parameter space and 3 of Klüver's 4 form constants in the gallery must be manually imposed.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:769-783 — in branch_selection_for, roll_stable tests 2*gamma_3(theta) > gamma_0 only at the preset's rendering angle pattern_angle_deg (clipped to [15, 75] deg) instead of across all theta (or theta_opt ~ 45 deg), falsely reporting roll_stable=True in bressloff_v1_metrics.csv lines 9, 10, and 12 whenever pattern_angle_deg is 0, 60, or 90 deg.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:931-959 — in stability_scan, when params.pattern != 'auto' and params.parity differs from critical_branch (e.g. fig29_* and fig30_* where parity='even' but critical_branch='odd'), branch_selection_for evaluates the even eigenfunction at the odd branch's critical_q and critical_growth.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:954-958 — setting wave_number_qstar = critical_q / hypercolumn_mm (with d_hyp = 2.0 mm and gallery q* = 1.4475) produces a cortical wavelength lambda_c = 8.68 mm (11 cycles on the 97.9 mm torus), 3.1x longer than Bressloff et al.'s (2002 §1.1) 2.4-3.2 mm (30-36 stripes), and only quantizes |k| rather than (k_x, k_y), leaving non-integer azimuthal cycles k_y*L/(2*pi) = 11*sin(theta) and a 9.9x left-meridian seam on oblique/spiral modes.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] README.md:431-442 — the ### [2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py] documentation is out of sync with the script: it claims 10/11 fixture checks pass (omitting the 122 runs[].checks with 11 failures), states that both hemispheres carry a bilateral-mirror mode by default (now full-field), attributes the contoured hex FFT shift to sqrt(3)k instead of 2k, and describes a 4x4 figure / 4-preset GIF / 17 self-test checks instead of the actual 4x5 figure / 5-preset GIF / 22 self-test checks and --sweep/--preset/--hemifield-mode flags." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.677"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

